        {
            "_id": "0dcWuh8VCmVaFUYH",
            "img": "systems/pf2e/icons/actions/Passive.webp",
            "name": "Proof of Undeath",
            "sort": 600000,
            "system": {
                "actionType": {
                    "value": "passive"
                },
                "actions": {
                    "value": null
                },
                "category": "defensive",
                "description": {
                    "value": "<p>A sanctum knight believes themself to be a living immortal, but if offered proof that they are in fact undead, they must succeed at a @Check[will|dc:20] save or become @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Frightened]{Frightened 1} (or @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Frightened]{Frightened 3} on a critical failure). On a critical success, they're temporarily immune to this fear for 24 hours. Once they recover from being frightened, their memories of the proof offered fade and they once again regard themselves as living immortals. Proof of undeath includes whenever they take vitality damage, whenever they restore HP as a result of void damage, or whenever a character within 30 feet presents evidence or an argument as a 2-action activity with the linguistic trait and succeeds at a @Check[deception|dc:17], @Check[diplomacy|dc:17], or @Check[intimidation|dc:17] check.</p>"
                },
